## PART II: TWO BOOT PATHS

### BIOS (Legacy)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| Boot sector | 512 bytes at LBA 0 |
| Load address | `0x7c00` |
| Initial mode | 16-bit Real Mode |
| Complexity | Simpler, more control |
| Hardware | Older machines, VMs |

### UEFI (Modern)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| Boot format | PE executable (like Windows .exe) |
| Initial mode | 32-bit or 64-bit (already protected/long) |
| Features | Graphics, filesystem, network before OS loads |
| Complexity | More setup, more capability |
| Hardware | All modern machines |

**Decision for Zion:** Start with BIOS for learning/VM testing. Port to UEFI for real hardware deployment.

